4d:["$","$L4b",null,{"title":"Cache entries vanish after a restart even though the disk is intact","id":"cache-entries-vanish-after-a-restart-even-though-the-disk-is-intact","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["The boot scan only deletes files whose names it cannot parse as a store key;\neverything else is re-added, and the eviction policy then runs against the\nwhole set, so a store over ",["$","code",null,{"children":"max_bytes"}]," or ",["$","code",null,{"children":"max_count"}]," is trimmed at startup.\nSeparately, switching the digest function between ",["$","code",null,{"children":"sha256"}]," and ",["$","code",null,{"children":"blake3"}],"\n(",["$","code",null,{"children":"default_digest_hash_function"}]," on the server, ",["$","code",null,{"children":"--digest_function"}]," on the\nclient) does not delete anything, but every lookup misses because clients now\ncompute different digests. See ",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/configuration/stores","children":"Stores"}],"."]}]}]
